      "components": [
        { "id": "TXT1", "type": "draw/text", "x": 2, "y": -28, "props": { "text": "6502 ROM and RAM", "size": "title", "font": "sans" } },
        { "id": "TXT2", "type": "draw/text", "x": 2, "y": -25, "props": { "text": "A W65C02S CPU (U1) runs the program in the AT28C256 EEPROM (U2) and keeps a count and its\nstack in the 62256 SRAM (U3), wired as in Ben Eater's 6502 computer:\n  •  ROM at $8000–$FFFF: U2 is enabled while A15 is high.\n  •  RAM at $0000–$3FFF: U3 is enabled while A15 is low and the clock PHI2 is high (one\n     74HC00, U4); A14 enables its outputs only in the lower 16 KB.\nX1 clocks the CPU at 1 kHz. R1 holds RESB high until RESET (SW1) pulls it low; R2–R6 hold\nRDY, IRQB, NMIB, BE and SOB high. DS1–DS4 show the address bus in hex.\n\nRun (F5), then press and release RESET: the CPU reads the reset vector at $FFFC–$FFFD,\njumps to $8000 and runs the program listed on the right, a count in RAM. In the Memory tab,\nU3's byte $0010 counts up once every 34 cycles, $0200 copies it, and $01FE–$01FF hold the\naddress JSR pushed. The Waveforms tab records the clock, RESB, SYNC, RWB and both buses.", "size": "large", "font": "sans" } },
        { "id": "TXT3", "type": "draw/text", "x": 58, "y": -28, "props": { "text": "; The program in the ROM, U2, as the CPU sees it:\n; ROM byte n is at address $8000 + n. The number\n; after each ; is the instruction's clock cycles.\n\n                        .org $8000\n8000  A2 FF     reset:  LDX #$FF     ; 2  stack pointer: $01FF\n8002  9A                TXS          ; 2\n8003  64 10             STZ $10      ; 3  count := 0\n8005  E6 10     loop:   INC $10      ; 5  count += 1\n8007  A5 10             LDA $10      ; 3  A := count\n8009  20 10 80          JSR store    ; 6  pushes $800B\n800C  80 F7             BRA loop     ; 3\n800E  FF FF                          ;    erased, never run\n8010  48        store:  PHA          ; 3  save A\n8011  8D 00 02          STA $0200    ; 4  copy the count\n8014  68                PLA          ; 4  restore A\n8015  60                RTS          ; 6  back to $800C\n                                     ; 34 cycles a count\n\n                        .org $FFFC\nFFFC  00 80             .word reset  ;    the reset vector", "size": "large", "font": "mono" } },
